<% content_for :title, "Sign in" %>

<div class="signin">
  <h1>Sign in</h1>
  <p class="signin__why">
    codegym keeps your attempts so you can see what you have done and how long
    it took. GitHub is the only way in, and it is asked for nothing beyond your
    public profile.
  </p>

  <%# A button, not a link: the request phase is POST so that
      omniauth-rails_csrf_protection can check the authenticity token.
      turbo: false because this submission has to be a real browser navigation.
      Turbo would submit it with fetch, and the response is a redirect to
      github.com, which fetch cannot follow cross-origin -- it fails CORS
      before the user ever sees GitHub. %>
  <%= button_to "Continue with GitHub", github_auth_path,
        class: "button", form: { data: { turbo: false } } %>

  <p class="signin__back"><%= link_to "Back to the library", root_path %></p>
</div>
